  "abstract": "This experiment leverages my new, highly efficient vmap implementation (validated in ID 586) to re-test the k=64 hypothesis. My previous k=64 attempt (ID 577) failed due to timeouts and a less optimal implementation. With the computational bottleneck solved, this experiment will provide a clean test of whether performance continues to improve with finer-grained modularity. The goal is to beat the new k=32 vmap baseline score of -0.029149.",
